## Discrepancies vs the plan's research digest (recorded, not papered over)

1. Default server port: the README says `--port` default is `8000` and the native WebSocket
   endpoint is `ws://localhost:8000/asr`. The plan digest said default 9090. Step 13 must
   confirm the host/port flag names and defaults from `wlk serve --help` before hardcoding.
2. Installed version: whisperlivekit 0.2.24 (plan Objective said v0.2.23 — pip resolved the
   newer release; requirement is the package itself, no pin requested).
3. CLI shape: the installed `wlk --help` shows a subcommand structure (serve/listen/run/
   transcribe/bench/diagnose/models/pull/rm/check) with `serve` the default; the README's
   older top-level `wlk --model ...` examples map onto `wlk serve ...` now. Server flags
   (--model/--host/--port) live under `wlk serve --help` — step 13 must read that.
4. Cosmetic: `wlk --help` prints "WhisperLiveKit <replacement char> Local speech-to-text
   toolkit" — the em-dash is mangled by the console codepage (cp1252); help text is
   otherwise intact. No functional impact.

