## PS 5.1 gotcha fixed in scripts/setup-wlk.ps1 (why the script is written this way)

1. `pip.exe install --upgrade pip` fails on Windows ("To modify pip, please run the following
   command") — pip refuses to replace its own console-script exe. Must use
   `python -m pip install --upgrade pip`. The first run hit this and aborted; the script now
   uses the `python -m` form and is idempotent (venv creation skipped on re-run).
2. Under `$ErrorActionPreference='Stop'`, PS 5.1 treats native stderr as a terminating error
   (NativeCommandError). Every native call is followed by `2>&1` + an explicit $LASTEXITCODE
   check so the script fails on real exit codes, not on stderr noise.